    "body": "## Problem\n\n`vim.filetype.add()` extension mappings match only the text after the final dot, but the documentation does not say so.\n\nCloses #40044\n\n## Solution\n\nDocument that behavior and regenerate `runtime/doc/lua.txt`.\n\nAI-assisted: OpenAI Codex. This remains Draft pending the required human review.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-18T08:29:54Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "For the future please see [the AI PR contributing guidelines](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#pull-requests-prs). The code looks mostly fine, but having vibe-coded prs myself, I can tell that the PR description seems is entirely auto-generated without human review. We do not need to see that `make lintdoc` had 0 errors :sweat_smile: \r\n\r\nAlso, if this is ready, please mark as such.",
